        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "<p dir=\"ltr\">I am writing, my master and mentor \u2014 may God in his mercy lengthen your life, preserve your health and happiness, and avert evil from you \u2014 from home, with 11 remaining in Elul, may God seal it fo[r you and for us] with the best seal. I am in a state of health and grace, thank God, Lord of the Two Worlds. After the arrival of your letter, I read in it of your well-being and your health, and thanked God for it. I cannot describe to you, sir, how much I am seized with longing for you. I ask God in his mercy to bring our meeting near. I delivered your letter to my master the Rav, may God preserve his greatness, and he was pleased with it. He prays for you. He read me your letter and informed me of what had happened to you, praised be the One who saves the deserving. Your well-being, thanks and gratitude to God, made me happy. I sent you my letter containing one to my master Ab\u016b Mu\u1e25ammad Q\u0101sim, may the Lord help him. I was wounded by what you did to me. It is only that I considered you dearer than a brother, and what you did was not what I would have hoped for from you. Nothing is more serious (upsetting?) for me than the oath which you have had me give. But, my master, this world is a house of blessing and recompense. He who gives service gets service; the server is served. I would like you to please hand over my purse to Ab\u016b Mu\u1e25ammad\u00a0Q\u0101sim. It contains 80 dinars, a quarter, and a q\u012br\u0101t. The [din]ars belonging to my master and mentor Abu \u2019l-Far[aj] you must not pay over. If they come from you, and are used for exchange [ ] It would be better if you change them to dirhems. If you pay him in low-quality ones (waraq), so much the better. If not, for God\u2019s sake, do not give him a single dinar from them. If possible, mix them with the purse of my maternal uncle. If you spend them, buy a load of flax with them, it doesn\u2019t matter whether scutched or hatchelled.</p>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">My chest is tight (waiting) for the arrival of your letters with what you have done. Also, I would like it if you would please watch over Q\u0101sim as he purchases. I want you to say to him: \u201cif foreign, it must be of the very highest quality, if B\u016b\u1e63\u012br\u012b, the good, that is, from 4 to 3\u00bd or around that.\u201d As for what you will want to know, my master: that over here the ships had been detained. Olive oil was at 42, but went down to 31; soap was [ ]; lead was 3 rising to 4; tar is 4; western (Maghrib\u012b) goods all went up. The authorities seized the wax in d\u0101r \u02bfAbd and seized my uncle\u2019s wax among it. I do not know how or when a price will be fixed for it. This very day Mard\u016bk\u2019s letter arrived; he says that 3 boats from Sicily arrived and 2 of our associates arrived in them. They set off from al-Mahdiyya 41 days ago. We hear it reported that they left behind 6 ships loading, and they are in a hurry. They remained detained until al-Tifl\u2019s boat came, then they set off. I have informed you of this. A letter from the elder my maternal uncle, may God help him, arrived from Tinn\u012bs. Their arrival in Tinn\u012bs was on Tuesday, a day before Nayr\u016bz (Coptic New Year). A letter arrived for you from my maternal uncle; it is enclosed in my letter.</p>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
